        "For a family in Sankeshwar the decision is not abstract, because it has a cost in distance. Staying on the state board or CBSE means the child studies in town or in Belagavi and competes through KCET, NEET or CUET-UG, all of which are well-understood routes here with plenty of local coaching. Choosing IGCSE and then the Diploma generally means a hostel in Kolhapur or Bengaluru, or the private candidate route, and the family should be clear about which of those it is signing up for.",
        "Neither direction is better in general and we will not pretend otherwise. If a student wants medicine in India, the state board or CBSE plus serious NEET preparation is the more direct road and we say so to parents who were hoping for a different answer. If the family is thinking about a university in the United Kingdom, Canada, Australia, Germany or Singapore, or expects to move abroad again, then IGCSE and the Diploma fit far better and the earlier the switch the easier it is.",
