        "Four things move the number. The course and level first, because a Physics HL or Mathematics AA HL specialist has a narrower pool and more preparation behind each hour than a Class 7 mathematics tutor. Rarity second: Psychology, Environmental Systems and Societies, Computer Science or a self-taught literature course sit higher than Economics or Biology simply because fewer people have taught them. Weekly hours third. Proximity to a May or November session fourth, since exam-period work is denser to prepare.",
        "Comparing this with local tuition needs care or it misleads. A neighbourhood batch in Sankeshwar or Hukkeri is inexpensive because twenty or thirty students share one teacher and because it teaches the state board or PU syllabus, which is a different product rather than a cheaper version of the same one. The fair comparison is a private IB specialist in Kolhapur, Belagavi or Pune, where a family would also be paying for travel, for time on the highway, and quite often for a hostel.",
        "If the budget is fixed, say so at the start and we will shape something to fit rather than quote and hope. A block of eight sessions on one weak topic, a single subject taken online instead of three, or a paired lesson with a classmate on the same course and level are all normal arrangements here, and all of them are quoted in writing before they begin.",
