        "Inside India, the Association of Indian Universities treats the IB Diploma as equivalent to the Class 12 certificate, which is what makes an Indian university application possible at all. That equivalence is the starting point and not the finish: individual universities set their own subject requirements and minimum grades, and a student who dropped mathematics entirely will find several engineering and economics courses closed regardless of equivalence.",
        "The entrance examinations each have their own rules and they change. CUET-UG accepts students from IB and IGCSE backgrounds under its registration conditions and is now the route into a large number of central universities. JEE Main has conditions on the mathematics, physics and chemistry a candidate must have studied. NEET sets its own biology, physics and chemistry requirements. KCET, the Karnataka route that most families in this district know best, has its own eligibility and domicile conditions which an IB candidate should read in the current bulletin rather than assume.",
        "Locally, the institutions a Sankeshwar family already knows are in Belagavi and across the border. Visvesvaraya Technological University has its headquarters in Belagavi, Rani Channamma University is there, and the KLE group's medical and engineering colleges draw students from across the district. Karnatak University at Dharwad and the Hubballi engineering campuses are a few hours south, and Shivaji University at Kolhapur is closer than any of them for a family already looking into Maharashtra.",
